WEBVTT

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.290
Taegeuk refers to the source of everything in the universe

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:36.290
and the universal law in which everything continuously goes through cycles of creation and destruction.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:42.290
Taegeuk Yukjang stands for Gang and symbolizes the endless flow of water and its flexibility.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.290
Taegeuk Yukjang is the final stage of the intermediate course

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.290
and is characterized by a smooth and flexible connection

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.290
when performing moves in succession or changing direction.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:58.290
We will now take a look at the Poomsae of Taegeuk Yukjang.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:02:00.500
Taegeuk Yukjang consists of five key moves.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
These are the key moves of Taegeuk Yukjang.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.000
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Taegeuk Yukjang.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.700
Sonnal Olgul Bituromaki is a technique used to perform Olgul Bakanmaki

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:37.700
using the performance thrusting foot and the opposite hand blade.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:43.700
First, twist your torso about 45 degrees from the Apgubi posture.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.700
Your arms should cross and pass in front of your face

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.700
and Bakanmaki performed with the tip of your hands facing upward.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.700
Your blocking arm should cross outside your assisting arm.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:01.700
Be careful not to let your hand blade move outside the end of the line from your shoulder.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:09.300
The knee of your hind leg should not bend, and your sole must not leave the ground.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.860
Golyochanki is a technique used to spin and kick a target.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.860
Your kicking foot draws an arc outside in.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.860
Use the top of your foot and ball to strike the target.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.860
After kicking a target, perform a spinning kick by twisting your torso

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.860
as if you're spinning your shoulder on the same side backwards.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:45.280
Bakanmaki is a technique used to block, defend your face inside out using your wrist.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.280
Your blocking arm should cross past your face from outside your assisting arm

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.280
to perform the Bakanmaki.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:04:03.480
Your elbow should point downward, your fist upward, and at a philtrum elevation.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:10.300
Be careful not to let your blocking wrist move outside the end of the line from your shoulder

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.300
when performing the move.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:20.300
Arehechomaki is a technique used to block the lower body by crossing your arms in an X formation.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:25.300
It begins with your arms crossed in an X formation in front of your chest.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:32.300
Lower your arms to your lower abdomen, then block the lower part of your body from both sides.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.300
When blocking your lower body, your arms should straighten naturally,

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.300
and the space between your fist and legs should be about two raised fists length.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:48.300
Also, the back of your hammer fist and your front thigh should be aligned when seen from the front.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:56.300
Batangson-anmaki is a technique used to block, defend the torso inward by using the palm of your hand.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:01.300
Raise the fist of your assisting arm slightly to your solar plexus level.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:07.300
Your blocking hand should start about one hand length above your shoulder to block inward.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:11.300
When blocking, the palm of your hand should be placed in front of your solar plexus,

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.300
and your armpit should be touching your body.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:20.380
Your elbow should point downward.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.380
Block by pulling the elbow of your blocking arm to your body,

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:32.770
and pull the elbow of your assisting arm at the same time, brushing the waist.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.770
These are the key moves of Taeguk-yukjang.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.770
We will now look at the moves in succession, connecting each move.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:43.770
The key moves of Taeguk-yukjang, first part, consist of

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:53.770
oren aremaki, oren abjagi, and wen pakkatmaki, and wen abjagi, and oren momtong pakkatmaki.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.770
Bend your knee after performing abjagi.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:02.770
Then perform preparatory pakkatmaki by crossing both arms in front of your chest.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:06.770
Complete the maki by touching the ground with your kicking foot.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:12.770
Concentrate on naturally connecting the two moves when training.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:16.770
Cautions for Taeguk-yukjang, first part, taking a closer look.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:23.770
When performing duiro doradiki, by spinning 180 degrees from oren duikkubi,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.770
shift your weight to your left leg.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:30.770
Spin using the ball of your foot as an axis, then set your foot.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:36.770
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk-yukjang, first part, in succession, while watching the video.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:51.200
The key moves of Taeguk-yukjang, second part, consist of

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:58.200
oren bituro maki, oren doryo chagi, and wen pakkatmaki, and oren jirugi.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:01.200
Oren abjagi, and wen jirugi.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.200
Oren pakkatmaki, and wen jirugi.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.200
Wen abjagi, and oren jirugi.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.200
And are haecho maki.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:17.870
After performing oren doryo chagi,

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:24.870
set your foot so the tip of your kicking foot points in the direction of progression about one and a half steps forward.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:32.870
Then, set your left foot 90 degrees to the left and perform pakkatmaki and oren jirugi in succession.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:37.870
After abjagi, bend your knee and perform preparatory jirugi.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.870
Then complete jirugi when the kicking foot touches the ground.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:49.270
Cautions for Taeguk-yukjang, second part, taking a closer look.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:54.270
When setting your kicking foot forward after doryo chagi,

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:59.130
your steps should not be too narrow.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:03.130
When your arms cross during are haecho maki,

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:09.460
the inside-outside of your arms must switch.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:15.460
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk-yukjang, second part, in succession while watching the video.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:40.870
The key moves of Taeguk-yukjang, third part, consist of

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.870
oren bituro maki,

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.870
wen doryo chagi, and oren aremaki,

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.870
wen apchagi, and oren pakkatmaki,

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:55.870
wen aremaki, and oren apchagi, and wen pakkatmaki.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:09:02.870
After performing wen doryo chagi, set your kicking foot about one and a half steps forward.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.870
Set your right foot backwards,

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:09.870
then spin your torso to the right.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:14.870
Perform oren aremaki by spinning and setting your foot backwards in one move

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.870
using the ball of your left foot as an axis.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.870
Bend your knee after apchagi,

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:28.340
then perform preparatory pakkatmaki by crossing your arms in front of your chest.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:31.340
Complete maki by setting your kicking foot.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:38.030
Always keep in mind that the two moves should connect naturally.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:47.610
Cautions for Taeguk-yukjang, third part, taking a closer look.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:53.610
Always remember that moves consisting of two or three consecutive moves

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:58.140
must connect naturally without any break.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:02.140
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk-yukjang, third part,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:18.040
in succession while watching the video.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:22.040
The key moves of Taeguk-yukjang, fourth part, consist of

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:26.040
oren sonnal godoromaki, oren sonnal godoromaki,

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:30.040
wen patang son anmakki, and oren jirugi,

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:35.580
and oren patang son anmakki, and wen jirugi.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:40.580
Shift your weight to your left foot from the previous move.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.580
Set your right foot 90 degrees to the right,

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:48.580
then perform wen sonnal godoromaki and jirugi.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.580
Next, shift your weight to your right foot.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:54.580
Set your left foot back, twist your torso,

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:58.580
then take the preparatory sonnal makki posture.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.580
At the same time, your left heel should also point

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:04.580
in the direction of your set back foot.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:08.580
Place the palm of your hand in front of your solar plexus.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.580
Be careful not to let your armpits move away from your body,

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:17.240
and your elbows should point downward.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:24.830
Quickly transition to jirugi after performing patang son makki.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:31.580
Set your foot backwards in a straight line.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:36.580
Cautions for taeguk yukjang, fourth part, taking a closer look.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:41.580
When assuming the baro posture, move your front foot backwards.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:45.580
When stepping back, the foot moving back should set first

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:49.580
and not draw an arc in the process.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:57.260
Be careful not to overdo the spin the moment your foot touches the ground.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.260
We will now practice the moves of taeguk yukjang,

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:16.200
fourth part in succession while watching the video.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.200
This concludes the training for taeguk yukjang.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:13:23.300
We will take another look at the moves and master poomsae.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.300
We have looked at the key moves of taeguk yukjang

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.300
and provided thorough explanations for each move

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.300
and things to watch out for.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:33.300
Please continue with your training,

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:36.300
reminding yourself of the flexibility of water

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.300
which symbolizes taeguk yukjang,

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:42.300
concentrating on the natural flow of the moves.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.300
We'll see you again in the taeguk jirjang video.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.300
Thanks for watching.

